		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5201&amp;p=37632#p37632"><![CDATA[
The problem with this display brightness on the 10W radios has been discussed extensively on this forum and IIRC is actually a hardware 'feature' on these radios, so that even with the official firmware the display is not as bright on the 10W radios as it is on the 5W radios.<br><br><br>You must however load the 10W compatible firmware, because the signal that turns backlight on / off is controlled from a different pin on the MCU/CPU. Hence why the 5W radio firmware won't work on the 10W radio.<br><br>There isn't a firmware fix that can make it any brighter.  <br><br>The only way to mask the issue is to create a theme with colours that are higher contrast. <br><br>IMO the default black&amp;white theme is probably already the highest contrast available, but you could try different contrasting colours<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Jul 02, 2025 10:44 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
